    (v_test, 1, $q$NON_VERBAL$q$, 2, NULL, 13, $q$Rotation$q$, $q$Three eighths of a turn$q$, $q$rotation$q$, $q$Which option shows the figure turned 135° clockwise?$q$, $q$svg$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 90 90" width="90" height="90"><g transform="translate(5,5)"><rect x="0" y="0" width="80" height="80" rx="6" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#9ca3af" stroke-width="1.5"/><polygon points="40,10 52,34 46,34 46,66 34,66 34,34 28,34" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="58" cy="58" r="6" fill="#1f2937"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$svg$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><g transform="rotate(45 40 40)"><polygon points="40,10 52,34 46,34 46,66 34,66 34,34 28,34" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="58" cy="58" r="6" fill="#1f2937"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><g transform="rotate(135 40 40)"><polygon points="40,10 52,34 46,34 46,66 34,66 34,34 28,34" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="58" cy="58" r="6" fill="#1f2937"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><g transform="rotate(-135 40 40)"><polygon points="40,10 52,34 46,34 46,66 34,66 34,34 28,34" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="58" cy="58" r="6" fill="#1f2937"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><g transform="translate(80,0) scale(-1,1)"><g transform="rotate(135 40 40)"><polygon points="40,10 52,34 46,34 46,66 34,66 34,34 28,34" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="58" cy="58" r="6" fill="#1f2937"/></g></g></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><g transform="rotate(225 40 40)"><polygon points="40,10 52,34 46,34 46,66 34,66 34,34 28,34" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="58" cy="58" r="6" fill="#1f2937"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$B$q$, $q$135° is one and a half right angles. The arrow, which pointed up, now points to the bottom right, and the dot moves from the bottom right round to the left side.$q$),
